\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let $H_n$ be the first clause count at which sequential independent uniformly signed proper 3-clauses make an n-variable formula unsatisfiable. Are there absolute $c,C>0$ such that $cn\leq Var(H_n)\leq Cn$ for all sufficiently large n?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let $H_n$ be the first clause count at which sequential independent uniformly signed proper 3-clauses make an n-variable formula unsatisfiable. Are there absolute $c,C>0$ such that $cn\leq Var(H_n)\leq Cn$ for all sufficiently large n?

